{"availability":"available","full":"cl4cnam/funcSug","name":"funcSug","description":"FuncSug is a simple alternative to event-driven programming and game loops. No main loops or event-action associations any more thanks to concurrency, waiting for specific events and a special handling of interruptions.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":16,"forks":0,"created":"2022-01-28T16:40:41Z","updated":"2026-08-28T18:31:04Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://github.com/cl4cnam/funcSug/wiki","topics":["async-await","await-event","easy-programming","event-loop","gui-programming","logical-parallelism","programmer-friendly","programming-language","structured-concurrency","user-event","user-interaction"],"demo":"https://cl4cnam.github.io/try_FuncSug/?example=drinkingCow","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T11:03:08.454Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T11:03:08.454Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T11:03:08.454Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T11:03:08.454Z","stars":16,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["When a branch is finished the other branch is definitively interrupted","Many people ask why GUI programming is so difficult. Some of common difficulties come from event-driven programming problems. That's why, with FuncSug, programmers do NOT have to follow the event-driven programming paradigm. For example, you no longer link an event to an action (like \"addEventListener\" does) and so no longer have the corresponding problems."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cl4cnam/funcSug/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b2f0462401f3012e6b73ea1e53673d32ed93464aebca92da4dabe8a26fb84e1c","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T11:03:08.659Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T11:03:08.659Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"When a branch is finished the other branch is definitively interrupted","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cl4cnam/funcSug/blob/main/README